<!--
    Toolbars of the factory's own Project table (MdmFactory.xsd). the product owner's decision, 2026-09-22 16:40
    (PLAN.md "Decisions prises"): Cockpit and Proposal review are things done BEFORE the master table is
    generated, so they belong on Project - not on the master tables (that is a separate lot, on branch
    feature/master-toolbars / fix/master-toolbar-module-services; see docs/MASTER-ZONE.md sec 12).
    Referenced from MdmFactory.xsd's Project table via
    <tabularViewTop>FactoryProjectTableTop</tabularViewTop>, <tabularViewRow>FactoryProjectRow</tabularViewRow>,
    <recordTop>FactoryProjectRecordTop</recordTop> (tools/xsd_emitter.py, T('Project', ..., toolbars={...})).
    A referenced toolbar fully REPLACES EBX's default one (no "extend default" mechanism), so the table-top
    and record-top toolbars re-declare the standard "+" Create then the Actions menu first, mirroring
    CtbDefaultToolbar.getDefaultTableTop and the shipped example
    ebx-assistant/WEB-INF/ebx/schemas/mcp-servers-administration_1.0_toolbars.xml verbatim for that part.
    Separators between every button keep them from being rendered as one linked group (that shipped
    example's own comment says so too).

    FactoryCockpit and ProposalReview are schema-extension services of THIS SAME model (MdmFactory.xsd,
    ebx.ui.FactoryCockpitServiceDeclaration / ProposalReviewServiceDeclaration, ServiceKey.forName - bare
    names, never <module>@<xsdPath>@<service>): a toolbar of model X can only name X's own schema services
    bare, or MODULE-level services as module@Service - never a schema-extension service of a DIFFERENT
    model (CLAUDE.md sec 6 "A DMA model's toolbars..."; confirmed live and the hard way on the master
    toolbars lot, docs/MASTER-ZONE.md sec 12.8: the bare/qualified forms both failed there because that
    toolbar lives on the MASTER model, a different schema than MdmFactory.xsd). Here the toolbar and the
    services share the same model, so the bare name is correct and no serviceParameters are needed at all -
    FactoryCockpit is UserServiceDeclaration.OnRecord and ProposalReview is OnTableView, both activated
    directly on /root/Project, so EBX resolves the launching record/selection from the toolbar's own
    context, exactly like ProposalReviewServiceDeclaration's own javadoc describes
    ("the project is then resolved from whatever record is selected").

    Row toolbar (FactoryProjectRow, TABLE_VIEW_ROW): no default part - a row toolbar decorates an
    already-visible record, real examples on this instance never give it one (see e.g.
    ebx-ps-profiling-web/WEB-INF/ebx/schemas/profiling_result_toolbars.xml, toolbar "indicatorResult") -
    just the two buttons, ICON_ONLY, separator between them (two-button row toolbar with a separator: see
    ebx-cs-mima-web/WEB-INF/ebx/schemas/MigrationManager_toolbars.xml, toolbar id 1).
-->
